title: POST /repos/:repo/duplicates/scan
tags: Duplicates
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: Starts a duplicate scan as a background task; the result is a summary, and reading the groups is an ordinary query.

Asynchronous, like reconcile: `202 Accepted` with `{"task_id": "<32hex>"}`, or
`409 Conflict` when a duplicate scan is already pending or running for this
repository. Follow it through the task endpoints (spec-tasks).

Body, all optional:

|!Key |!Default |!Meaning |
|`min_size` |`1` |files smaller than this are skipped (`1` excludes empty files) |
|`rehash` |`false` |ignore every stored hash and recompute |
|`metarecord` |— |32-hex: scan only that metarecord's subtree |

The task's result is a summary, never a listing:

```
{"groups": 128, "files": 291, "reclaimable": 4823710720,
 "hashed_partial": 5540, "hashed_full": 412, "skipped": 3}
```

There is no listing endpoint: the groups are read with `POST /query`
([[Finding duplicates]]).

Everything duplicate detection added to the wire was additive — this endpoint, a
task kind, `mfr_*` fields, the `same` query — so it needed no `API_VERSION` bump.
A newer client talking to an older daemon gets a `400`/`404`, which it should
report as "this daemon does not support duplicate detection".
